From d47de1c7ad19d32c8853bbd31c2f9fc380e9c33c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium M9 Agent <agent@pandemonium.dev>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(sim): pop chase orders whose target died (M9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The M8 AI-vs-AI flagship never resolved because the armies froze mid-
match: an Order::AttackUnit whose commanded target died was never
popped (movement.rs documents that pop as the combat pipeline's job,
but no code ever did it), so the unit kept reporting Moving while
movement resolved no destination, requested no path, and the stuck
detector skipped its empty path — frozen forever, still shooting
whatever entered acquire range. Both sides' defense orders outlived
their intruders, both armies parked, and the wave machine's
'army >= 3' liveness check read the frozen camps as an active press.

Combat stage 1 now pops a head AttackUnit order whose target is gone
(covering every removal path: combat deaths, node depletion), resets
the runtime path, and the queue behind it advances. Two unit tests pin
the pop and the queue-advance; the M8-flagship-stall test documents
the diagnosis.

The M7 flagship golden moved with the fix (orders are canonical
hashed state; tick 0 is unchanged) and is re-pinned with this written
reason in tests/ai.rs, tests/match_rules.rs, and the tools winner-
field test — the demo golden (0x9d5ba9b565060336) is untouched: its
lone Attack command is gate-refused on the trivial world.
